# Kubeapply

Apply the currently open Kubernetes YAML from Sublime Text 4, with hard safety locks.

## Commands (Cmd+Shift+P / Ctrl+Shift+P)

| Command | What it does |
|---------|----------------|
| **Kubeapply: Apply Open File** | Pick context → namespace if needed → dry-run + diff + confirm → `kubectl apply` |
| **Kubeapply: Dry-Run Open File** | Read-only: context/namespace prompts → server-side dry-run (never creates namespaces) |
| **Kubeapply: Diff Open File** | Read-only: context/namespace prompts → `kubectl diff` (never creates namespaces) |
| **Kubeapply: Open Settings** | User settings |

## Hard safety locks (cannot be disabled)

- Always pass explicit `--context` (picker always matches kubectl target)
- Always run `kubectl apply --dry-run=server` before real apply
- Always require quick-panel confirmation before apply
- Never pass `--force` / `--force-conflicts`
- Always apply a **frozen buffer snapshot** (temp file), never a potentially stale on-disk path
- One interactive flow at a time
- Refuse apply when resource existence could not be verified (`block_on_unverified_resources`)
- Dry-Run / Diff **never** create namespaces (Apply may, after confirm)

## Flow (Apply)

1. Parses the open **buffer** (multi-doc YAML; no PyYAML required).
2. Quick-panel of **kubectl contexts**.
3. If a namespaced kind has no `metadata.namespace`, pick/type a namespace (injected into the temp YAML — not via `kubectl -n`).
4. Verifies target namespace(s) exist; if missing, prompts **Create namespace** (Apply only).
5. Before apply:
   - Warn on unsaved buffer
   - Extra gate for contexts matching `*prod*` / `*prd*` / `*live*` (type context name)
   - `kubectl get` to classify CREATE vs UPDATE (unverified → block)
   - Server-side dry-run (blocks on failure)
   - Diff tab before confirm when updating
   - Confirm (+ second confirm on overwrite)
   - Secret resources noted in the summary (plaintext may appear in tabs)

**macOS / ST4 note:** Interactive confirms use `quick_panel` / report tabs. Native sheets after `new_file` can hard-exit ST4.

## Settings

Preferences → Package Settings → Kubeapply

| Setting | Notes |
|---------|--------|
| `dangerous_context_patterns` | Extra type-to-confirm contexts |
| `block_on_unverified_resources` | Default true — refuse apply on UNKNOWN existence |
| `warn_secret_resources` | Default true |
| `show_diff_before_apply` | Default true |

## Requirements

- Sublime Text 4
- `kubectl` on PATH (or set `kubectl_path`)
